              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Julie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great recipe! To change things up I use tomato, cucumber, red onion, feta cheese and a little italian dressing."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KatBox"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Light and delicious on a hot summer day! I love pretty, colorful dishes, so I used Cherubs and Sunbursts (small yellow tomatoes). After peeling the cucumber, I scored lengthwise with a fork then cut lengthwise 4 times to slice quarters. Be sure to rip, not chop, the cilantro to preserve the beautiful leaves. And, I am a Spice Girl, so I added a variety of spices to my taste. Served in a glass bowl to show it off and it was a hit! I look forward to making it again as I want to experiment with variations. Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2016-07-23T15:00:02.540Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rock_lobster"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Cucumber Tomato Red Onion Salad Haiku: \"Lovely as written! Cool, colorful, and easy. Lots can be added.\" Great recipe for a summertime BBQ side dish. Definitely letting it chill in the fridge for several hrs. b4 serving makes it all the better. I've made this many times now, occasionally adding a little EVOO, balsamic vinegar, roasted corn, cumin, black beans -- really, as a base, it's fantastic, but it's equally fun and delicious to make by jazzing it up w/ other goodies.",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-10T15:15:10.060Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "froggylaurie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My husband made this for us with our veggies from the garden. He added a splash of balsamic vinegar &amp; toasted sesame seeds! I'm addicted to it, by itself it is wonderful. On top of a plate of greens to make a fresh green salad is great, too (i use baby spinach). The juices combined with the vinegar make a delicious light dressing and it is so quick to put together! Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-11T12:43:36.550Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RoseAle2140"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Refreshing and easy! Half I just put the cukes and tomatoes with French vinaigrette for the teen and made the other half as directed and added a little cracked black pepper and garlic powder. Delish!",
            "datePublished": "2025-07-27T21:45:48.528Z"
          },
          {
